Subject: [PATCH] Keep asynchronous frame receive sockets nonblocking and alive

The HAL reader can remain inside a blocking management nl_recvmsgs after
AP reconfiguration closes that socket. The descriptor may even be reused,
leaving authentication and timer processing stalled for every radio.
Publish asynchronous sockets only after switching them to nonblocking mode.
Use the existing recursive hostapd lock for descriptor snapshots, management
and spurious dispatch, registration and teardown, but never across select.
An empty nonblocking receive is normal, not a reason to reopen the socket.

Upstream-Status: Pending

